  "description": "Alpha.3 hardware-discovered WiFiS3 telemetry-cache performance hotfix on top of commit 885718d and the V7 chunked-response candidate. The V7 hardware tests proved correct 401 and 200 responses without bridge lockup, but measured 2.75 s for a short auth failure, 6.86 s for a 266-byte console stats response, and 9.63 s for the 1457-byte status response. V8 retains maximum 512-byte response writes while removing synchronous remoteIP lookups from polling/auth-failure paths, caching WiFi connection/IP/RSSI telemetry, processing HTTP before periodic NTP and telemetry modem commands, and rate-limiting unsynchronised NTP retries. Header-first authentication, measured query fallback, production isolation, and application version 5.0.0-alpha.2 remain unchanged.",
